`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- The manuscript rests on one identity: Cauchy-Binet applied to a bordered closed-loop system matrix. It makes every closed-loop numerator and the full characteristic polynomial linear in the controller's Plücker coordinates. I checked the signs independently with a Schur complement.
- For m=p=2 the big chart of Gr(2,4) is cut out by the single relation t=ad-bc. DDP synthesis then becomes classifying the real points of one quadric restricted to an affine subspace. The result is correct but elementary.
- The four-state example shows exactly what goes wrong if decomposability is dropped (linear relaxation) or if complex solutions are accepted. In both cases the test reports feasibility when no real gain exists.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

